                <pb facs="0958" n="859" sameAs="frus:frus1936v05/pg859"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">834.00/794: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Howard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Asunción</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-02-19T16:00:00-04:00">February 19, 1936—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 20—11:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>21. Colonel Franco arrived at Asunción at 3 o’clock. It is understood that he
                    traveled in a plane chartered by the Buenos Aires newspaper <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Crítica</hi>. It is probable that efforts to form a
                    provisional government will begin at once.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Buenos Aires.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Howard</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
